{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1549002-building-the-local-darkness-for-my-city","id":1549002,"title":"Building the local darkness for my City","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-03-06T00:59:54-08:00","id":1549002,"title":"Building the local darkness for my City","content":"Building my city in North Colorado with some friends for fun, working slowly from mortals up. Cults, locations, maybe people? Wondering what else we could build collaboratively or take inspiration from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28042-rexitonic","name":"Rexitonic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28042_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-06T06:00:29-08:00","id":1549010,"title":"","content":"Depends on what you're aiming for. Have you got a theme and/or mood in mind? Is the primary type of challenge the PCs are intended/intending to deal with more investigative, social, or action-oriented? Have the players got any specific types of monsters or antagonists (gameline-focused or otherwise) that they're interested in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-06T08:50:20-08:00","id":1549013,"title":"","content":"I would look up Kelly Armstrong's Other World series as a possible source for building up your supernatural community and how they interact with each other and how they keep themselves hidden from the mundane world.<br /> <br /> Another ther is Mick Farren vampire series that focuses on a small &quot;family&quot; of undead and how scary they would be and how the gap between us and them would be greater as they would see as tools to be used and discarded when needed.<br /> <br /> Though I don't know if you can find his books via online orders?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 03-06-2025, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-06T12:08:31-08:00","id":1549018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1549002-building-the-local-darkness-for-my-city?p=1549010#post1549010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on what you're aiming for. Have you got a theme and/or mood in mind? Is the primary type of challenge the PCs are intended/intending to deal with more investigative, social, or action-oriented? Have the players got any specific types of monsters or antagonists (gameline-focused or otherwise) that they're interested in?</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling is the biggest interest from the group so far, definitely more on the social and investigative side of interest as well. Gonna talk more in depth about with them tomorrow night when we meet and see what else could be of interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28042-rexitonic","name":"Rexitonic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28042_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-06T13:49:17-08:00","id":1549022,"title":"","content":"Then maybe some of Fables comic series would be a good source of inspiration for Changeling The Lost or even Stephen Blackmoore novels. Perhaps even watching some Once Upon A Time from ABC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-06T14:46:20-08:00","id":1549025,"title":"","content":"Depending on how comprehensible (versus terror of the unknowable) you're aiming for, tying a freehold of changelings to some other local strangeness could serve as a solid connective tissue (whether at the scale of associating novel Courts with them or simply &quot;the Winter Court has a vested interest in a specific local funeral home where an unusual number of fetches' remains have been found by a local graverobber&quot;).<br /> <br /> Figuring out the degree of conspiracy and/or deeply mysterious weirdness in your setting will also be useful, because it lets you determine how to tilt social and investigative approaches to the darkness in question. Chronicles is pretty well set up for specimens of published entities to stay fairly consistent in their context, but an alien thing in a well that a cult has worked out how to use to work miracles in exchange for esoteric and bloody-handed payment is a different beast from a dreamweaving folk song serving as the vehicle for the ghost of an ancient witch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-06T17:07:23-08:00","id":1549032,"title":"","content":"I definitely love and try to lean into the weird and bizarre.<br /> What I'm thinking is we're gonna set up everything on a very basic level, then I'll slide in the mysteries and darkness behind it all.<br /> <br /> Honestly thinking of doing non-seasonal courts here, but I'll have to see how my players feel about that one.<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28042-rexitonic","name":"Rexitonic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28042_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-06T17:07:53-08:00","id":1549033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1549002-building-the-local-darkness-for-my-city?p=1549022#post1549022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then maybe some of Fables comic series would be a good source of inspiration for Changeling The Lost or even Stephen Blackmoore novels. Perhaps even watching some Once Upon A Time from ABC.</div> </div> </div> </div> Any recommendations from Fables?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28042-rexitonic","name":"Rexitonic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28042_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-06T17:29:24-08:00","id":1549034,"title":"","content":"Nothing that comes to mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-06T21:02:39-08:00","id":1549042,"title":"","content":"I forget to mention that Zenescope Comics had a fantasy line and I liked the version of The Pied Piper story, Robin Hood and a different track on Dante's Inferno.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 03-07-2025, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-07T16:06:50-08:00","id":1549059,"title":"","content":"Some suggestions if you do Seasonal Courts. In our game we had the Winter Court having their fingers in the construction and real estate market as they buy or build safehouses.<br /> <br /> The Spring Court owned a luxury hotel and casino and a couple of nightclubs <br /> The Summer Court having interests in boxing \ud83e\udd4a clubs and gyms and the local police department.<br /> <br /> We had a hard time with the Autumn Court. Now we would use the Sun and Moon Courts if we ever go back to the setting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-08T02:20:33-08:00","id":1549069,"title":"","content":"They sounded interested in Astrological courts actually could be fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28042-rexitonic","name":"Rexitonic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28042_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-13T15:40:08-07:00","id":1549268,"title":"","content":"Northern Colorado eh? Well, the closest I've been is living up in SLC, so, Colorado is bear country; and by bears, I mean The People. As for cults, well, you got a lot of Wolf-Blooded families up there; you can tell because they got, like, a dozen children running around. I tend to go with which books I have; I got Second Sight, but never picked up Mage: the Awakening (I should have, but I liked Ascension too much). So, there's yer cult(s). And there should be plenty of Spirits running around (I got the Book of Spirits). My experience in up there leads me to believe everyone is on drugs. And sorry, I'm not big on Changeling, so I can't suggest anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-13T16:43:25-07:00","id":1549276,"title":"","content":"In our game we are building up the city of Calgary as it's our province largest city and in many ways is seen as a twin for Denver Colorado. We use it for Vampire and Mage The Awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-26T00:56:50-07:00","id":1549577,"title":"","content":"All the stuff helps. I actually completed a four courts for our area, I'll have to post em in the Changeling sub forums","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28042-rexitonic","name":"Rexitonic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28042_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T20:12:55-07:00","id":1550825,"title":"","content":"Are you basing the city off of a real city in Northern Colorado? If so, look up that real-city's sister-city; they should have one and use the myths and legends of the sister-city to spice it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-09T13:31:57-07:00","id":1550891,"title":"","content":"I am, didn't think of that will definitely do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28042-rexitonic","name":"Rexitonic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28042_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}